但现在随着年龄增长，就变成了，我没染发根。

639
00:27:30.180 --> 00:27:30.440
No.
没错。

640
00:27:31.240 --> 00:27:35.040
I've got some grays and the back of my head's a hot mess.
我长了一些白发，后脑勺简直一团糟。

641
00:27:35.180 --> 00:27:35.640
Put on a hat.
戴上帽子。

642
00:27:36.160 --> 00:27:38.360
Those are the three reasons I put a hat on today.
这就是我今天戴帽子的三个原因。

643
00:27:38.680 --> 00:27:40.020
Well, I think you look really cute.
嗯，我觉得你看起来真的很可爱。

644
00:27:40.200 --> 00:27:41.640
I think it looks cute too.
我也觉得看起来很可爱。

645
00:27:42.380 --> 00:27:43.040
All right.
好了。

646
00:27:44.060 --> 00:27:45.600
Time for the Amper Show.
Amper秀时间到了。

647
00:27:45.600 --> 00:27:46.200
I know.
我知道。

648
00:27:46.540 --> 00:27:52.240
That's my, um, another one of the characters I can do for any of the voiceover folks listening.
这是我，嗯，我可以为任何收听节目的配音人士表演的另一个角色。

649
00:27:52.580 --> 00:27:54.080
Can you sustain that?
你能保持这个声音吗？

650
00:27:54.460 --> 00:27:55.580
Sure I can.
当然可以。

651
00:27:55.720 --> 00:27:56.560
Oh, you can.
哦，你可以的。

652
00:27:56.740 --> 00:27:57.620
You really can.
你真的可以。

653
00:27:57.780 --> 00:27:58.560
Hey, Ange.
嘿，安吉。

654
00:27:58.780 --> 00:28:01.500
I mean, write the show for her, please.
我是说，请帮她写那个节目。

655
00:28:02.000 --> 00:28:02.580
All right.
好吧。

656
00:28:02.880 --> 00:28:08.440
For real, we open with Nellie in the conference room with Aaron and Pete.
说真的，我们以奈莉在会议室和亚伦、皮特在一起的场景开场。

657
00:28:08.440 --> 00:28:14.940
Yeah, apparently Aaron and Pete are part of this social media initiative that Nellie
是的，显然亚伦和皮特参与了奈莉发起的这个社交媒体计划。

658
00:28:14.940 --> 00:28:15.640
has set up.
她发起的。

659
00:28:15.720 --> 00:28:19.220
So they're trying to have an online presence for Dunder Mifflin.
所以他们正试图为邓德·米夫林公司建立在线形象。

660
00:28:19.440 --> 00:28:19.620
Yeah.
是的。

661
00:28:19.780 --> 00:28:24.100
They've created a fake profile for a really cool guy named Derek McBlack.
他们为一个叫德里克·麦克布莱克的酷炫家伙创建了一个虚假档案。

662
00:28:24.500 --> 00:28:26.620
And I guess it's just Pete in sunglasses.
我猜那其实就是戴着墨镜的皮特。

663
00:28:27.060 --> 00:28:32.960
And they're trying to get likes and followers and they're creating fake accounts to get those.
他们试图获得点赞和关注，并为此创建了虚假账号。

664
00:28:32.960 --> 00:28:38.040
And at the same time, they're just being flirty and super cute.
与此同时，他们表现得非常轻浮且超级可爱。

665
00:28:38.260 --> 00:28:42.120
And Nellie says, I consider myself a genius for putting the two of them together.
奈莉说，我把自己把他们俩凑在一起视为天才之举。

666
00:28:42.420 --> 00:28:49.620
First of all, I just want to say kudos to our writers for making Nellie's job a job.
首先，我想对我们的编剧表示赞赏，是他们让奈莉的工作看起来像份正经工作。

667
00:28:50.000 --> 00:28:50.460
Right.
没错。

668
00:28:50.460 --> 00:28:53.160
She really does have special projects.
她确实有特别项目要做。

669
00:28:53.640 --> 00:28:56.600
Now, do we need these special projects?
那么，我们需要这些特别项目吗？

670
00:28:57.100 --> 00:28:57.260
Right.
对吧。

671
00:28:57.440 --> 00:28:58.360
Probably not.
可能不需要。

672
00:28:58.580 --> 00:28:58.760
Right.
没错。

673
00:28:58.760 --> 00:29:02.540
But, you know, the social media initiative, special projects.
但是，你知道，社交媒体计划，特别项目。

674
00:29:03.180 --> 00:29:04.080
Makes it legitimate.
这让它看起来名正言顺。

675
00:29:04.420 --> 00:29:05.060
All right.
好吧。

676
00:29:05.140 --> 00:29:06.660
We had a fan question from Chris W.
我们收到了一位来自英国新森林的粉丝克里斯·W的提问。

677
00:29:07.060 --> 00:29:09.080
from the New Forest, England.
来自英国新森林。

678
00:29:09.540 --> 00:29:13.880
When Aaron and Pete are working on their grand social media initiative, they set up a fake
当亚伦和皮特在进行他们宏大的社交媒体计划时，他们建立了一个虚假

679
00:29:13.880 --> 00:29:15.560
profile for Derek McBlack.
档案，叫德里克·麦克布莱克。

680
00:29:16.100 --> 00:29:20.180
Aaron informs Nellie that Derek is, in fact, just Pete in sunglasses.
亚伦告诉奈莉，德里克其实就是戴着墨镜的皮特。

681
00:29:20.720 --> 00:29:26.620
We only get a brief glimpse of McBlack, but I'm not convinced this is Pete in sunglasses.
我们只瞥见了麦克布莱克一眼，但我并不确信那是戴着墨镜的皮特。

682
00:29:27.240 --> 00:29:30.320
Would the real Derek McBlack please stand up?
真正的德里克·麦克布莱克能站出来吗？

683
00:29:30.880 --> 00:29:32.540
I didn't think it looked like Pete either.
我也觉得那看起来不像皮特。

684
00:29:33.400 --> 00:29:34.260
Me either.
我也这么觉得。

685
00:29:34.840 --> 00:29:39.740
I reached out to Steve Burgess, and Steve said, Chris, you're right.
我联系了史蒂夫·伯吉斯，史蒂夫说，克里斯，你是对的。

686
00:29:39.840 --> 00:29:41.600
That doesn't look like Jake.
那看起来不像杰克。

687
00:29:44.180 --> 00:29:46.740
Steve said, I don't have any info.
史蒂夫说，我没有任何相关信息。

688
00:29:46.740 --> 00:29:50.380
I'm pretty sure we didn't ever take a picture of Jake.
我很确定我们从来没给杰克拍过那张照片。

689
00:29:50.640 --> 00:29:55.260
My guess is it's a stock photo that the art department picked of a guy in sunglasses.
我猜那是美术部门选的一张戴墨镜男人的库存照片。

690
00:29:55.960 --> 00:29:56.980
Good catch, Chris.
观察得很仔细，克里斯。

691
00:29:56.980 --> 00:29:57.440
I totally agree.
我完全同意。

692
00:29:57.640 --> 00:29:57.800
Yeah.
是的。

693
00:29:58.200 --> 00:30:00.140
Here's one little catch in this scene.
这个场景里还有一个小细节。

694
00:30:00.320 --> 00:30:02.840
Did anyone else notice that Jake Lacey has a cold?
还有人注意到杰克·莱西感冒了吗？

695
00:30:03.500 --> 00:30:04.340
I didn't.
我没注意到。

696
00:30:04.520 --> 00:30:04.740
Yeah.
是的。

697
00:30:04.860 --> 00:30:06.080
He has a cold in this episode.
他在这一集里感冒了。

698
00:30:06.240 --> 00:30:06.960
How do you know?
你怎么知道的？

699
00:30:07.120 --> 00:30:07.720
For sure.
非常确定。

700
00:30:08.100 --> 00:30:09.500
He's like, yeah, exactly.
他就像是，对，没错。

701
00:30:09.800 --> 00:30:11.780
He's like, this is my cold.
他就像是说，这是我的感冒。

702
00:30:11.920 --> 00:30:12.740
That's what he sounds like.
他听起来就是那样。

703
00:30:12.840 --> 00:30:14.440
He's like, come on, guys.
他就像是说，拜托了，伙计们。

704
00:30:15.020 --> 00:30:17.420
He literally says that in the conference room later.
他后来在会议室里真的说了这句话。

705
00:30:17.600 --> 00:30:18.340
He's like, come on, guys.
他就像是说，拜托了，伙计们。

706
00:30:18.380 --> 00:30:19.200
What's this all about?
这到底是怎么回事？

707
00:30:19.200 --> 00:30:26.320
Well, I did not notice this, but I just want to say, you can do person with cold voiceover.
嗯，我没注意到这一点，但我只想说，你可以做那种感冒嗓音的配音。

708
00:30:26.360 --> 00:30:26.880
Thank you.
谢谢。

709
00:30:27.000 --> 00:30:27.860
Put it on my resume.
把它写进我的简历里吧。

710
00:30:28.080 --> 00:30:28.200
Yep.
没错。

711
00:30:28.920 --> 00:30:33.360
Erin's going to have a talking head where she's giddy about getting to work with Pete.
艾琳会有一个采访镜头，她在镜头里对能和皮特一起工作感到非常兴奋。

712
00:30:33.600 --> 00:30:37.480
She talks about how well they work together, and she gets all flustered.
她谈到他们合作得有多好，然后变得非常慌乱。

713
00:30:38.000 --> 00:30:38.340
Yeah.
是啊。

714
00:30:38.740 --> 00:30:38.960
Yeah.
是啊。

715
00:30:38.960 --> 00:30:40.440
She's clearly sweet on him.
她显然对他有意思。

716
00:30:40.560 --> 00:30:40.720
Yeah.
是啊。

717
00:30:40.780 --> 00:30:46.520
She's like, you know, I mean, I probably work well with a girl or a guy or someone I'm into.
她就像是说，你知道，我的意思是，我大概和女生、男生或者我喜欢的人都能合作得很好。

718
00:30:46.620 --> 00:30:47.340
Not that I'm into Pete.
并不是说我喜欢皮特。

719
00:30:47.460 --> 00:30:47.720
Ah!
啊！

720
00:30:47.720 --> 00:30:48.460
Yes.
是的。

721
00:30:48.840 --> 00:30:49.960
She's very cute in it.
她在里面非常可爱。

722
00:30:50.240 --> 00:30:52.400
Next up, we see Jim at Athlead.
接下来，我们看到吉姆在Athlead公司。

723
00:30:52.640 --> 00:30:58.600
We find out that one of their biggest investors has requested a lunch meeting, and he just says,
我们发现他们最大的投资者之一要求开个午餐会，而他只是说，

724
00:30:58.680 --> 00:31:00.520
hey, guys, is it cool if we just do it a little early?
嘿，伙计们，我们稍微提前一点开会可以吗？

725
00:31:00.540 --> 00:31:02.640
Because remember, I have to get back to Scranton today.
因为记住，我今天得赶回斯克兰顿。

726
00:31:03.100 --> 00:31:04.080
And they're like, sure.
他们就说，当然可以。

727
00:31:04.220 --> 00:31:04.800
Yeah, no problem.
没问题。

728
00:31:05.020 --> 00:31:05.160
Yeah.
是啊。

729
00:31:05.420 --> 00:31:07.060
And then Jim has his talking head.
然后吉姆有了他的采访镜头。

730
00:31:07.220 --> 00:31:09.680
He's very excited about Cece's ballet recital.
他对西西的芭蕾舞表演感到非常兴奋。

731
00:31:10.060 --> 00:31:14.620
He's taught her a signature move, the Cece spin and kiss, and he demonstrates it.
他教了她一个招牌动作，西西旋转加飞吻，他还演示了一遍。

732
00:31:14.740 --> 00:31:16.040
He's a very cute dad moment.
这是一个非常可爱的爸爸时刻。

733
00:31:16.040 --> 00:31:21.860
But I absolutely love the guy who is walking in the background of this talking head.
但我绝对喜欢那个在采访镜头背景里走过的人。

734
00:31:22.120 --> 00:31:22.340
Oh, no.
噢，不。

735
00:31:22.720 --> 00:31:23.760
Did you see him?
你看到他了吗？

736
00:31:23.880 --> 00:31:25.200
I watched it three times.
我看了三遍。

737
00:31:25.340 --> 00:31:26.420
No, I didn't see him.
不，我没看到他。

738
00:31:26.420 --> 00:31:27.300
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

739
00:31:27.400 --> 00:31:29.300
It's such good background acting.
这背景表演太棒了。

740
00:31:29.300 --> 00:31:41.860
He's walking by, and Jim does the spin and the kiss, and he just kind of looks in to the conference room as you would if someone was spinning and whatever for a camera.
他走过去的时候，吉姆做了旋转和飞吻的动作，他就像正常人看到有人在镜头前旋转什么的，往会议室里看了一眼。

741
00:31:42.140 --> 00:31:43.860
It's very good job.
干得非常漂亮。

742
00:31:44.120 --> 00:31:46.800
Very, very good job to the person who did this cross.
那个做这个穿行表演的人干得非常、非常漂亮。

743
00:31:47.220 --> 00:31:49.800
Well, now we're going to set up a Daryl Dwight storyline.
好了，现在我们要铺垫一条达里尔和德怀特的故事线。

744
00:31:50.240 --> 00:31:51.740
Daryl arrives to Dunder Mifflin.
达里尔来到了邓德·米夫林公司。

745
00:31:51.860 --> 00:31:53.260
He has an athlete bag.
他背着一个Athlead的包。

746
00:31:53.580 --> 00:31:56.140
And Dwight immediately is like, why do you have that?
德怀特立刻就问，你为什么背着那个？

747
00:31:56.280 --> 00:31:56.660
Why are you?
你为什么……？

748
00:31:56.780 --> 00:31:59.360
And he calls the company Stumpany, a.k.a.
他还把这家公司称为“笨司”，也就是，

749
00:31:59.520 --> 00:32:00.160
Stupid Company.
笨蛋公司。

750
00:32:00.360 --> 00:32:01.220
That really made me laugh.
那真的把我逗笑了。

751
00:32:01.340 --> 00:32:02.340
It made me laugh, too.
我也被逗乐了。

752
00:32:03.160 --> 00:32:06.000
This is when Daryl tells Dwight that he's going to work for Stumpany.
这一段是达里尔告诉德怀特他要去“树干公司”工作。

753
00:32:06.440 --> 00:32:06.720
Uh-huh.
嗯哼。

754
00:32:06.940 --> 00:32:08.100
Dwight is shocked.
德怀特震惊了。

755
00:32:08.280 --> 00:32:09.100
He's so mad.
他气坏了。

756
00:32:09.240 --> 00:32:09.900
He calls Jim.
他给吉姆打了电话。

757
00:32:09.900 --> 00:32:10.440
He's furious.
他怒不可遏。

758
00:32:10.640 --> 00:32:12.540
He's like, hey, Halpert, what's the big idea?
他就像是说，嘿，哈珀特，你到底在搞什么鬼？

759
00:32:12.540 --> 00:32:13.940
First, you jumped ship.
先是你跳槽了。

760
00:32:14.140 --> 00:32:15.400
Now you're stealing Daryl, too.
现在你还要把达里尔也挖走。

761
00:32:15.600 --> 00:32:16.580
When will it end?
这什么时候才是个头？

762
00:32:17.020 --> 00:32:21.120
And Jim says, we'll take your worst fear and multiply it by infinity.
吉姆说，我们会把你最恐惧的事乘以无穷大。

763
00:32:21.600 --> 00:32:24.160
Dwight says, you won't stop until you've poached us all.
德怀特说，你们不把我们挖光是不会罢休的。

764
00:32:24.340 --> 00:32:26.360
And Jim goes, yeah, even you.
吉姆回道，没错，连你也不放过。

765
00:32:26.520 --> 00:32:29.480
And then here's one of my favorite lines from the whole entire episode.
接下来是整集中我最喜欢的台词之一。

766
00:32:29.640 --> 00:32:33.540
Dwight says, no, I'll be damned if I'm going to let us lose me.
德怀特说，不，我绝不会眼睁睁看着我们失去我。

767
00:32:33.840 --> 00:32:34.540
I know.
我知道。

768
00:32:35.380 --> 00:32:36.920
That made me laugh so hard.
那段真的把我笑死了。

769
00:32:38.180 --> 00:32:42.300
Well, now Pam is going to approach accounting because she needs to ask Angela,
好了，现在帕姆要去找会计部，因为她需要问安吉拉，

770
00:32:42.540 --> 00:32:46.160
if she's heard anything about the Irish-American Cultural Center mural.
看她有没有听说关于爱尔兰裔美国人文化中心壁画的事。

771
00:32:46.740 --> 00:32:47.980
Guess what, guys?
你们猜怎么着？

772
00:32:48.720 --> 00:32:56.340
Angela's husband, the senator, recommended Pam to be the artist for this big mural project in Scranton.
安吉拉的丈夫，那位参议员，推荐帕姆担任斯克兰顿这个大型壁画项目的艺术家。

773
00:32:56.500 --> 00:32:58.520
Yeah, I loved this callback.
没错，我喜欢这个前后呼应。

774
00:32:58.820 --> 00:33:01.920
Remember, the senator had come to the office with coffee.
还记得吗，参议员曾带着咖啡来过办公室。

775
00:33:02.120 --> 00:33:02.860
During the Target.
在《目标》那一集里。

776
00:33:03.060 --> 00:33:03.740
During the Target.
在《目标》那一集里。

777
00:33:03.900 --> 00:33:05.020
It was in deleted scenes.
那是删减片段里的内容。

778
00:33:05.020 --> 00:33:10.880
And here we have this footage because the senator is looking for Angela but wants to talk to Oscar.
这里我们有这段素材，因为参议员在找安吉拉，但想和奥斯卡谈谈。

779
00:33:10.880 --> 00:33:13.260
And Daryl says, I think they're in the warehouse.
达里尔说，我想他们应该在仓库里。

780
00:33:13.600 --> 00:33:13.840
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

781
00:33:14.220 --> 00:33:18.280
So we've got this great footage of the senator noticing Pam making her mural.
所以我们有这段很棒的素材，参议员注意到了正在画壁画的帕姆。

782
00:33:18.680 --> 00:33:20.700
Pam has a talking head where she says,
帕姆有个采访镜头，她说，

783
00:33:20.900 --> 00:33:26.000
Senator Lipton, help me submit my design for a new mural on a downtown building.
利普顿参议员帮我提交了市中心大楼新壁画的设计方案。

784
00:33:26.300 --> 00:33:27.760
And she's waiting to hear.
她正在等消息。

785
00:33:28.100 --> 00:33:29.920
You know, she's trying to downplay it.
你知道，她试图表现得低调一点。

786
00:33:30.040 --> 00:33:32.460
She's like, I mean, there are so many people they would go with.
她说，我是说，有那么多人选。

787
00:33:32.520 --> 00:33:36.060
Why would they go with an unknown like me when they could have a big name like Tracy Fleab?
他们为什么会选我这种无名小卒，而不选特蕾西·弗利布这种大人物呢？

788
00:33:36.060 --> 00:33:37.340
Oh, Tracy Fleab.
哦，特蕾西·弗利布。

789
00:33:37.820 --> 00:33:40.520
Big time mural artist in Scranton.
斯克兰顿的大牌壁画艺术家。

790
00:33:41.000 --> 00:33:41.200
Yeah.
没错。

791
00:33:41.840 --> 00:33:45.060
I know for a fact that Greg likes funny names.
我敢肯定格雷格喜欢这种滑稽的名字。

792
00:33:45.400 --> 00:33:45.700
Yeah.
没错。

793
00:33:45.700 --> 00:33:47.600
And I feel like a bunch of names were pitched.
我觉得当时提议了很多名字。

794
00:33:47.620 --> 00:33:50.060
And they loved Fleab, Tracy Fleab.
他们很喜欢弗利布，特蕾西·弗利布。

