All right, here is the coffee order for the folks at Dunder Mifflin.
好了，这是邓德·米夫林员工们的咖啡订单。

1116
00:47:24.710 --> 00:47:26.950
Phyllis ordered a banana fruit smoothie.
菲利斯点了一杯香蕉果昔。

1117
00:47:27.950 --> 00:47:29.990
Stanley ordered a small decaf.
斯坦利点了一杯小杯低因咖啡。

1118
00:47:29.990 --> 00:47:33.510
Daryl ordered a double latte, lotsa latte.
达里尔点了一杯双份拿铁，多加奶。

1119
00:47:34.570 --> 00:47:39.050
Oscar ordered a venti kai, tea misto, half soy.
奥斯卡点了一杯超大杯茶拿铁，半份豆奶。

1120
00:47:39.850 --> 00:47:42.050
Kevin ordered a cappuccino.
凯文点了一杯卡布奇诺。

1121
00:47:42.880 --> 00:47:45.530
Is that different from a cappuccino?
那和卡布奇诺有什么区别吗？

1122
00:47:45.610 --> 00:47:48.630
I think it's what Kevin thinks is a cappuccino.
我觉得那是凯文以为的卡布奇诺。

1123
00:47:48.790 --> 00:47:50.310
He wrote, Captain Chino.
他写的是“船长奇诺”。

1124
00:47:51.170 --> 00:47:52.110
Okay, okay.
好吧，好吧。

1125
00:47:52.390 --> 00:47:54.970
Pete ordered a cappuccino with cinnamon.
皮特点了一杯加肉桂粉的卡布奇诺。

1126
00:47:56.110 --> 00:47:59.770
Clark ordered a tall and black like my women.
克拉克点了一杯中杯黑咖啡，就像我喜欢的女人一样。

1127
00:48:00.770 --> 00:48:05.670
Nellie ordered a black tea, any, with lemon like my men.
奈莉点了一杯红茶，随便什么牌子，加柠檬，就像我喜欢的男人一样。

1128
00:48:06.530 --> 00:48:10.950
Aaron ordered a vanilla blendy thing, five sugars, happy face.
亚伦点了一杯香草混合冰沙，加五份糖，画个笑脸。

1129
00:48:11.770 --> 00:48:14.670
Meredith ordered an Irish coffee, extra Irish.
梅雷迪斯点了一杯爱尔兰咖啡，多加点爱尔兰威士忌。

1130
00:48:15.850 --> 00:48:18.430
And this goes to your theory, Angela.
这正好印证了你的理论，安吉拉。

1131
00:48:18.770 --> 00:48:22.350
Creed ordered a pastrami on rye, fries, Coke, nothing to drink.
克里德点了一份黑麦面包熏牛肉三明治、薯条、可乐，没有饮料。

1132
00:48:22.690 --> 00:48:22.970
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1133
00:48:23.670 --> 00:48:24.110
Yeah.
没错。

1134
00:48:24.410 --> 00:48:25.130
There you go.
就是这样。

1135
00:48:25.430 --> 00:48:26.910
Angela did not order any.
安吉拉没点任何东西。

1136
00:48:27.150 --> 00:48:28.370
No, she didn't.
是的，她没点。

1137
00:48:29.550 --> 00:48:33.670
Angela Martin and Angela Kinsey don't want to be part of your coffee order.
安吉拉·马丁和安吉拉·金赛都不想参与你们的咖啡订单。

1138
00:48:33.930 --> 00:48:35.890
Angela Martin does not want to be stimulated.
安吉拉·马丁不想摄入咖啡因。

1139
00:48:36.510 --> 00:48:36.830
Mm-mm.
嗯嗯。

1140
00:48:37.690 --> 00:48:38.690
She doesn't.
她确实不想。

1141
00:48:38.990 --> 00:48:40.750
And Angela Kinsey doesn't drink coffee.
而且安吉拉·金赛不喝咖啡。

1142
00:48:40.870 --> 00:48:42.490
And Angela Kinsey doesn't drink coffee.
而且安吉拉·金赛不喝咖啡。

1143
00:48:43.290 --> 00:48:45.850
Dwight now bursts into the annex and he says,
德怀特冲进附楼，他说，

1144
00:48:46.090 --> 00:48:50.190
Clark, I need any complaints pertaining to Daryl in the past few weeks.
克拉克，我需要过去几周里所有关于达里尔的投诉。

1145
00:48:50.190 --> 00:48:53.030
I want it broken down by keywords.
我要按关键词分类。

1146
00:48:53.330 --> 00:48:56.030
And Clark's like, listen, that's going to be tough.
克拉克说，听着，这很难办。

1147
00:48:56.190 --> 00:48:57.230
We use Windows 95.
我们用的是Windows 95系统。

1148
00:48:58.090 --> 00:49:00.070
And Dwight's like, fine, just print it out.
德怀特说，行吧，那就直接打印出来。

1149
00:49:00.410 --> 00:49:04.030
Then this cuts to that hilarious dot matrix printer.
然后镜头切到那台搞笑的针式打印机。

1150
00:49:04.030 --> 00:49:07.090
That's like, key, key, key, key.
声音就像是，吱吱，吱吱，吱吱，吱吱。

1151
00:49:07.670 --> 00:49:08.810
Yeah, it's going to take forever.
是啊，这得花上好久。

1152
00:49:09.130 --> 00:49:13.310
And when we asked Kelly Cantley what memory she had from shooting this episode,
当我们问凯莉·坎特利对拍摄这一集有什么印象时，

1153
00:49:13.510 --> 00:49:15.370
this was one of the scenes she mentioned.
她提到了这一幕。

1154
00:49:15.670 --> 00:49:16.430
Here's what she said.
她是这么说的。

1155
00:49:17.310 --> 00:49:23.890
The scene where Dwight goes into Clark and tells him to print all the complaints.
德怀特走进克拉克办公室，让他打印所有投诉的那场戏。

1156
00:49:24.690 --> 00:49:29.970
I looked and looked at that scene and I could not figure out how it was going to be funny
我反复看了那场戏，怎么也想不出它好笑在哪里，

1157
00:49:29.970 --> 00:49:31.370
until we shot it.
直到我们把它拍出来。

1158
00:49:31.370 --> 00:49:38.270
And Matt's own brilliant operator dropped the camera down to just over the machine
马特的摄影师非常机智，把摄像机降到了机器上方，

1159
00:49:38.270 --> 00:49:40.690
onto Dwight and Clark.
正对着德怀特和克拉克。

1160
00:49:40.970 --> 00:49:43.550
And then I thought it was just so funny.
然后我就觉得这太搞笑了。

1161
00:49:43.730 --> 00:49:45.630
It makes me laugh every time I see it.
每次看我都忍不住笑。

1162
00:49:46.440 --> 00:49:51.190
I think this scene is so funny because it is the callback to Clark
我觉得这场戏之所以好笑，是因为它呼应了克拉克

1163
00:49:52.090 --> 00:49:56.530
being frustrated by our just dinosaur technology.
对我们那些老古董技术的沮丧。

1164
00:49:56.910 --> 00:49:57.130
Yeah.
没错。

1165
00:49:57.330 --> 00:49:58.430
Talk about old tech.
说到老技术。

1166
00:49:58.650 --> 00:50:00.430
He's surrounded by old tech.
他被老技术包围了。

1167
00:50:01.150 --> 00:50:04.790
Dwight is now going to hold a conference room meeting about customer loyalty.
德怀特现在要召开一场关于客户忠诚度的会议。

1168
00:50:05.150 --> 00:50:05.830
What is it?
那是什么？

1169
00:50:06.050 --> 00:50:07.250
Can you hold it in your hand?
你能把它拿在手里吗？

1170
00:50:07.550 --> 00:50:08.890
Can you dump it on a woman?
你能把它倒在女人身上吗？

1171
00:50:09.290 --> 00:50:10.910
No, because it's an idea.
不能，因为它只是个概念。

1172
00:50:11.170 --> 00:50:12.350
What does it mean?
那是什么意思？

1173
00:50:12.770 --> 00:50:16.310
This whole time a man has been sitting at the front of the conference room,
会议室前一直坐着一个人，

1174
00:50:16.410 --> 00:50:19.750
Dwight is now going to introduce him as Mr. Romenko,
德怀特现在要介绍他是罗门科先生，

1175
00:50:19.750 --> 00:50:24.570
a client of 20 years, who came in today enraged at Daryl,
一位合作了20年的客户，今天来的时候对达里尔大发雷霆，

1176
00:50:24.730 --> 00:50:27.930
who was distracted because he was working on outside projects.
因为达里尔当时忙于外部项目而分心了。

1177
00:50:28.130 --> 00:50:31.890
And Mr. Romenko is like, no, no, no, I wouldn't classify this as rage.
而罗门科先生却说，不不不，我不会把这称为愤怒。

1178
00:50:32.010 --> 00:50:33.390
He seems a bit confused.
他看起来有点困惑。

1179
00:50:33.630 --> 00:50:36.490
Well, there was a scene that would have come previous to this
其实在这之前本来有一场戏，

1180
00:50:36.490 --> 00:50:39.330
that sort of explains it all and set up the whole scene.
算是解释了这一切，并为整场戏做了铺垫。

1181
00:50:39.530 --> 00:50:41.510
In the shooting draft, it read like this.
在拍摄剧本里是这样写的。

1182
00:50:41.510 --> 00:50:45.910
A client, Mr. Romenko, a meek little man, enters the office tentatively.
客户罗门科先生，一个温顺的小个子男人，试探性地走进办公室。

1183
00:50:46.430 --> 00:50:47.390
Dwight spots him.
德怀特发现了他。

1184
00:50:47.750 --> 00:50:51.970
Dwight says, Mr. Romenko, right away, so sorry you felt the need to come in.
德怀特立刻说，罗门科先生，真抱歉让你觉得有必要亲自跑一趟。

1185
00:50:52.190 --> 00:50:54.470
Mr. Romenko says, I didn't.
罗门科先生说，我没觉得。

1186
00:50:54.650 --> 00:50:57.450
You called, but it's such a small matter.
是你打的电话，但这只是件小事。

1187
00:50:57.610 --> 00:50:58.490
Maybe we should juSt...
也许我们应该……

1188
00:50:58.490 --> 00:51:02.290
Dwight says, I understand, but we take customer loyalty very seriously here.
德怀特说，我明白，但我们非常重视客户忠诚度。

1189
00:51:03.030 --> 00:51:05.390
Emergency conference room meeting, everyone.
紧急会议，所有人到会议室来。

1190
00:51:05.890 --> 00:51:07.430
Mr. Romenko is like confused.
罗门科先生一脸困惑。

1191
00:51:07.670 --> 00:51:08.090
He's like, what?
他心想，什么？

1192
00:51:08.090 --> 00:51:12.670
And he turns to Mr. Romenko and says, I hope you have nothing planned for the whole afternoon.
然后德怀特转向罗门科先生说，希望你整个下午都没安排。

1193
00:51:13.650 --> 00:51:17.030
And Mr. Romenko says, actually, I do have.
罗门科先生说，其实，我有的。

1194
00:51:17.150 --> 00:51:21.670
And Dwight pushes Romenko into the conference room and then shouts to everyone,
接着德怀特把罗门科推进会议室，并对大家大喊，

1195
00:51:21.890 --> 00:51:23.770
irate customer coming through.
愤怒的客户来了。

1196
00:51:24.550 --> 00:51:24.850
Yes.
没错。

1197
00:51:25.210 --> 00:51:29.570
When we get back to the conference room, Daryl is going to say, I'm so sorry.
回到会议室后，达里尔会说，非常抱歉。

1198
00:51:29.570 --> 00:51:34.430
We were a day late on your delivery, but two of our trucks were down for repairs,
我们的送货晚了一天，因为有两辆卡车在维修，

1199
00:51:34.430 --> 00:51:36.810
and I don't see this ever happening again.
我保证以后绝不会再发生这种情况了。

1200
00:51:36.810 --> 00:51:40.050
And Mr. Romenko is like, fine, great.
罗门科先生说，行，太好了。

1201
00:51:40.050 --> 00:51:41.370
He's satisfied with that answer.
他对那个回答很满意。

1202
00:51:41.470 --> 00:51:42.290
He wants to leave.
他想离开。

1203
00:51:42.590 --> 00:51:43.750
Yeah, he's like, good for me.
没错，他觉得，这对我来说挺好。

1204
00:51:44.250 --> 00:51:46.870
Dwight's like, no, Mr. Romenko is angry.
德怀特觉得，不，罗门科先生很生气。

1205
00:51:47.070 --> 00:51:50.670
And Daryl forgot that loyalty is the key to relationships.
而达里尔忘了忠诚是人际关系的关键。

1206
00:51:51.410 --> 00:51:53.790
Well, Nellie is going to be like, I agree.
嗯，奈莉会说，我同意。

1207
00:51:54.150 --> 00:51:54.670
Yes.
是的。

1208
00:51:54.790 --> 00:51:57.630
She sees her way out now, and she's going to take it.
她现在看到了出路，她打算抓住它。

1209
00:51:57.810 --> 00:52:00.010
She says loyalty is everything,
她说忠诚就是一切，

1210
00:52:00.010 --> 00:52:04.990
and they should all ask themselves if they've been faithful in their relationships.
他们都应该问问自己，在人际关系中是否忠诚。

1211
00:52:05.810 --> 00:52:07.290
Stanley is like, uh-uh.
斯坦利觉得，呃，不行。

1212
00:52:07.490 --> 00:52:09.490
He's not going to participate in this conversation.
他不想参与这场谈话。

1213
00:52:10.090 --> 00:52:14.870
Nellie says Daryl is dating Dunder Mifflin but flirting with athlete on the side.
奈莉说达里尔在和邓德·米夫林公司交往，但私下里却在和运动员调情。

1214
00:52:15.070 --> 00:52:19.150
Then they start using Aaron as an example.
然后他们开始拿亚伦举例。

1215
00:52:19.370 --> 00:52:25.110
Like, what would it be like if Aaron, who is in a relationship with Andy,
比如，如果正在和安迪交往的亚伦，

1216
00:52:25.270 --> 00:52:28.910
was flirting with someone on the side, like maybe Creed?
私下里和别人调情会是什么样，比如克里德？

1217
00:52:28.910 --> 00:52:30.530
Creed and Creed's lying.
克里德，而且克里德在撒谎。

1218
00:52:30.730 --> 00:52:31.370
He's so funny.
他太搞笑了。

1219
00:52:31.490 --> 00:52:33.390
He's like, yeah, I'll play that out.
他说，好啊，我来演演看。

1220
00:52:33.870 --> 00:52:36.810
He's like, sure, yeah, let's see what, let's play that out.
他说，当然，好，让我们看看，让我们演演看。

1221
00:52:37.010 --> 00:52:42.290
And imagine during all of this, poor Mr. Romenko is just like, can I go?
想象一下，在这一切过程中，可怜的罗门科先生只是在想，我可以走了吗？

1222
00:52:42.990 --> 00:52:46.310
And this conference room scene was so fun to shoot.
这场会议室的戏拍起来太有趣了。

1223
00:52:46.530 --> 00:52:49.030
We broke and laughed several times,
我们中途笑场了好几次，

1224
00:52:49.030 --> 00:52:53.070
and I loved this little brief exchange between Angela and Aaron.
而且我很喜欢安吉拉和亚伦之间那段简短的对话。

1225
00:52:53.270 --> 00:52:53.950
I want to play it.
我想放出来看看。

1226
00:52:54.430 --> 00:52:57.350
Well, I think it would be immoral for Aaron to cheat on Andy.
嗯，我觉得亚伦背叛安迪是不道德的。

1227
00:52:57.550 --> 00:52:58.090
Oh, I'm sorry.
哦，抱歉。

1228
00:52:58.410 --> 00:52:59.530
Didn't you cheat on Andy?
你不是背叛过安迪吗？

1229
00:52:59.750 --> 00:53:01.570
Yes, and he didn't like it.
是的，而且他不喜欢那样。

1230
00:53:04.280 --> 00:53:05.000
That too.
那也是。

1231
00:53:05.200 --> 00:53:08.340
I love when you said yes, and he didn't like it very much.
我喜欢你说“是的，而且他不太喜欢”的时候。

1232
00:53:08.440 --> 00:53:10.600
Yes, and I'm really put out, and he didn't like it.
是的，我真的很不爽，而且他不喜欢那样。

1233
00:53:11.580 --> 00:53:14.600
One of our favorite things as a cast, we've talked about this before,
作为演员，我们最喜欢的事情之一，我们之前也聊过，

1234
00:53:14.840 --> 00:53:18.140
is to have a big group scene where everyone has a moment.
就是拍一场大群戏，让每个人都有表现的机会。

1235
00:53:18.360 --> 00:53:20.280
And this was one of those scenes.
这就是其中一场戏。

1236
00:53:20.560 --> 00:53:23.920
Everyone in the conference room had something hilarious that they contributed.
会议室里的每个人都贡献了非常搞笑的台词。

1237
00:53:23.920 --> 00:53:27.980
Yes, and by the way, Mr. Romenko was great.
是的，顺便说一下，罗门科先生演得太棒了。

1238
00:53:28.400 --> 00:53:32.220
Yes, guest star, shout out to Mr. Romenko, played by Bob Bluberman.
没错，客串明星，向罗门科先生致敬，由鲍勃·布鲁伯曼饰演。

1239
00:53:32.360 --> 00:53:36.740
He was originally a lawyer who left law to become an actor in 1995.
他原本是一名律师，1995年放弃法律转行做了演员。

1240
00:53:37.300 --> 00:53:39.880
Well, Bob has crossover connections with both you and I.
嗯，鲍勃和你我都有交集。

1241
00:53:39.940 --> 00:53:40.540
You want to hear them?
你想听听吗？

1242
00:53:40.760 --> 00:53:41.100
Yes.
想。

1243
00:53:41.520 --> 00:53:45.140
Bob and I have both had roles on Spin City and Strong Medicine.
鲍勃和我都在《城市大赢家》和《强力医疗》里演过角色。

1244
00:53:45.800 --> 00:53:51.400
And Angela, your crossover connections are Hot in Cleveland, New Girl, and Fresh Off the Boat.
安吉拉，你和他的交集是《魅力克利夫兰》、《杰茜驾到》和《初来乍到》。

1245
00:53:51.400 --> 00:53:54.040
Bob, we've worked on so many of the same shows.
鲍勃，我们合作过好多相同的剧集。

1246
00:53:54.320 --> 00:53:54.700
I know.
我知道。

1247
00:53:54.880 --> 00:54:01.160
He's appeared in over 100 TV shows, dozens of commercials, and voiceover spots.
他出演过100多部电视剧，几十个广告，还有配音工作。

1248
00:54:01.360 --> 00:54:01.840
Bob.
鲍勃。

1249
00:54:01.980 --> 00:54:02.860
Hook us up.
给我们牵线搭桥吧。

1250
00:54:02.980 --> 00:54:03.260
Yeah.
好啊。

1251
00:54:03.520 --> 00:54:04.560
We have so many voices.
我们有这么多声音。

1252
00:54:04.920 --> 00:54:06.100
We can do a lot.
我们能做很多事。

1253
00:54:06.460 --> 00:54:07.680
Hey, now, listen, Bob.
嘿，听着，鲍勃。

1254
00:54:07.800 --> 00:54:08.800
I got this guy, too.
我也找了这个人。

1255
00:54:08.980 --> 00:54:09.820
I can do this one.
我可以做这个。

1256
00:54:09.960 --> 00:54:11.320
He works at a tire shop.
他在一家轮胎店工作。

1257
00:54:11.880 --> 00:54:12.780
Tim's Tire Town.
蒂姆轮胎城。

1258
00:54:13.180 --> 00:54:18.200
I always say, if you're gonna get your beauty done, get your beauty done right.
我常说，如果你要打扮得漂漂亮亮，就得做得地道。

1259
00:54:19.000 --> 00:54:20.080
That's what she says.
她是这么说的。

1260
00:54:20.080 --> 00:54:20.880
See?
你看？

1261
00:54:21.060 --> 00:54:21.540
Look at us.
看看我们。

1262
00:54:21.680 --> 00:54:21.780
Bob.
鲍勃。

1263
00:54:22.200 --> 00:54:23.360
What can't we do?
有什么是我们做不到的吗？

1264
00:54:23.460 --> 00:54:23.740
Bob.
鲍勃。

1265
00:54:24.860 --> 00:54:25.740
Probably voiceover.
大概是配音吧。

1266
00:54:27.600 --> 00:54:30.180
Well, should we head on over to CeCe's Recital?
那么，我们要出发去西西的独奏会了吗？

1267
00:54:30.180 --> 00:54:31.620
Because it is underway.
因为已经开始了。

1268
00:54:32.520 --> 00:54:33.540
Yes, it is.
是的，开始了。

1269
00:54:33.600 --> 00:54:36.400
And I have a few more things to share about this day.
关于这一天，我还有几件事要分享。

1270
00:54:37.060 --> 00:54:42.580
Kelly had made sure I had the day off, so when we filmed these scenes, I could be there just right off camera.
凯莉确保我那天休假，所以当我们拍摄这些场景时，我就能待在镜头外。

1271
00:54:42.720 --> 00:54:43.760
You had to be.
你必须得在场。

1272
00:54:43.900 --> 00:54:44.520
I know.
我知道。

1273
00:54:44.520 --> 00:54:47.460
So, that morning, the girls got to go through hair and makeup.
那天早上，女孩们去做了发型和化妆。

1274
00:54:47.620 --> 00:54:48.560
They were very excited.
她们非常兴奋。

1275
00:54:48.700 --> 00:54:55.000
I have adorable pictures of these tiny little ladybugs in those big hair and makeup chairs, and they look so tiny in them.
我有这些小瓢虫坐在大大的化妆椅上的可爱照片，她们在椅子里看起来太小了。

1276
00:54:55.620 --> 00:54:59.080
Debbie and Sherry in hair and makeup took such great care of them.
负责发型和化妆的黛比和雪莉把她们照顾得很好。

1277
00:54:59.540 --> 00:55:02.880
And Isabel was already really familiar with the hair and makeup trailer.
伊莎贝尔对化妆车已经很熟悉了。

1278
00:55:03.000 --> 00:55:08.200
So, she was actually very excited that she got to sit in the chair and not just pop in and say hi to me.
所以，她其实非常兴奋能坐在椅子上，而不只是跑进来跟我打个招呼。

1279
00:55:08.200 --> 00:55:16.100
Well, what I loved about our hair and makeup folks, Angela, is that, you know, these little girls didn't really need hair and makeup.
安吉拉，我喜欢我们发型和化妆团队的一点是，你知道，这些小女孩其实并不需要化妆。

1280
00:55:16.360 --> 00:55:16.540
No.
没错。

1281
00:55:16.800 --> 00:55:18.380
But they fussed over them.
但他们对她们呵护备至。

1282
00:55:18.500 --> 00:55:18.920
Yes.
是的。

1283
00:55:19.100 --> 00:55:20.420
They made it an event.
他们把这变成了一场盛事。

1284
00:55:20.700 --> 00:55:23.660
This day was like a whole event for these little girls.
这一天对这些小女孩来说就像一场盛大的活动。

1285
00:55:23.860 --> 00:55:28.700
So, they would like maybe put their hair in a ponytail or pigtails or something, but they would linger.
他们可能会给她们扎个马尾辫或双马尾什么的，但他们会磨蹭很久。

1286
00:55:29.060 --> 00:55:29.340
Yeah.
是啊。

1287
00:55:29.500 --> 00:55:32.880
And they would brush their faces even if there wasn't any makeup on it.
即使脸上没化什么妆，他们也会给她们刷刷脸。

1288
00:55:32.940 --> 00:55:34.620
It was the cutest thing.
那真是太可爱了。

1289
00:55:34.820 --> 00:55:35.580
It was so cute.
太可爱了。

1290
00:55:35.580 --> 00:55:41.180
In fact, one time Isabel was on set, and I think I've shared this before, and I think my forehead was shiny.
事实上，有一次伊莎贝尔在片场，我想我之前分享过，当时我的额头有点油光。

1291
00:55:41.420 --> 00:55:43.460
They said, Angela, you have a little bit of shine.
他们说，安吉拉，你额头有点油光。

1292
00:55:43.600 --> 00:55:45.380
And they powdered my forehead.
于是他们给我的额头扑了粉。

1293
00:55:46.140 --> 00:55:51.220
So, Isabel walked into the hair and makeup, and she said to Sherry, can I get a little shine?
后来，伊莎贝尔走进化妆间，对雪莉说，我能弄点油光吗？

1294
00:55:51.480 --> 00:55:51.760
Yeah.
是啊。

1295
00:55:52.020 --> 00:55:53.740
Because she thought that was what you got.
因为她以为那是她们能得到的东西。

1296
00:55:54.220 --> 00:55:54.620
Yes.
是的。

1297
00:55:54.620 --> 00:56:00.200
And they just put their hair up in little ponytails, and then, you know, they got a tiny little bit of chapstick.
他们只是给她们扎了小马尾，然后，你知道，给她们涂了一点点润唇膏。

1298
00:56:00.480 --> 00:56:00.760
Yes.
是的。

1299
00:56:01.000 --> 00:56:01.980
And a little bit of shine.
还有一点点油光。

1300
00:56:02.720 --> 00:56:03.520
So sweet.
太贴心了。

1301
00:56:04.060 --> 00:56:08.700
Well, the location of this recital was the 20th Century Women's Club in Eagle Rock.
这场演出的地点是在鹰岩的二十世纪妇女俱乐部。

1302
00:56:08.940 --> 00:56:15.100
And I asked Steve Burgess, what was involved on the production end when you have a bunch of little kids on set?
我问史蒂夫·伯吉斯，当片场有一群小孩时，制作方面需要做些什么准备？

1303
00:56:15.120 --> 00:56:17.040
Because I know they can only work certain hours.
因为我知道他们的工作时长是有限制的。

1304
00:56:17.200 --> 00:56:18.140
They have to have breaks.
他们必须有休息时间。

1305
00:56:18.380 --> 00:56:19.600
They have to have tutors.
他们必须有导师。

1306
00:56:19.720 --> 00:56:21.320
They have to have a parent or guardian.
他们必须有父母或监护人陪同。

1307
00:56:22.020 --> 00:56:27.040
Steve said, since these were just three- and four-year-olds, they didn't really have to go to school.
史蒂夫说，因为这些孩子才三四岁，所以其实不需要去上学。

1308
00:56:27.040 --> 00:56:32.720
But they did have a school teacher there because it's required by California law.
但现场确实有一位学校老师，因为这是加州法律要求的。

1309
00:56:32.840 --> 00:56:34.740
But they didn't really make them go to school.
不过他们并没有真的强迫孩子去上课。

1310
00:56:34.860 --> 00:56:36.760
And that the shooting was very short.
而且拍摄时间非常短。

1311
00:56:37.060 --> 00:56:38.320
It was very short.
非常短。

1312
00:56:38.320 --> 00:56:42.060
And they did have a big room for everyone with chairs and the girls.
他们确实为所有人准备了一个大房间，里面有椅子和女孩们。

1313
00:56:42.280 --> 00:56:46.300
Like, I mean, literally, they had coloring books and crayons and little games.
我的意思是，他们真的准备了涂色书、蜡笔和小游戏。

1314
00:56:46.300 --> 00:56:47.700
And we all hung out together.
我们都在一起消磨时光。

1315
00:56:48.180 --> 00:56:56.400
And when I rewatched the episode with my daughter and we watched the dancing, she's right in the middle at the very first opening shot.
当我陪女儿重温那集节目看舞蹈表演时，她就在第一个开场镜头的正中间。

1316
00:56:56.400 --> 00:56:57.620
It's her and Maya.
是她和玛雅。

1317
00:56:57.780 --> 00:56:59.400
And they're right in the middle next to Cece.
她们就在西西旁边，处于正中间。

1318
00:57:00.160 --> 00:57:04.500
And she's like, oh, Mom, Maya knew the dance perfectly.
她说，哦，妈妈，玛雅把舞步记得一清二楚。

1319
00:57:04.660 --> 00:57:08.560
And when we watched, we both got tickled because Isabel got distracted by her shoes.
当我们看的时候，我们俩都乐了，因为伊莎贝尔被她的鞋子分散了注意力。

1320
00:57:08.560 --> 00:57:10.080
She looks down at her feet.
她低头看着自己的脚。

1321
00:57:10.200 --> 00:57:10.460
Aw.
噢。

1322
00:57:12.020 --> 00:57:13.300
And she was like, what am I doing?
她当时好像在想，我在干什么呢？

1323
00:57:13.380 --> 00:57:14.740
And I was like, well, you did love shoes.
我就说，好吧，你确实很喜欢鞋子。

1324
00:57:14.740 --> 00:57:15.520
I don't know.
我不知道。

1325
00:57:15.700 --> 00:57:17.260
Maybe you were looking at your shoes.
也许你当时是在看你的鞋子。

1326
00:57:17.560 --> 00:57:24.260
And there was an extra scene that they did with the little gals where they all poke their heads around the big curtain before they go on stage.
还有一个小女孩们的额外场景，她们在上台前都从大幕布后面探出头来。

1327
00:57:24.620 --> 00:57:27.940
That one didn't make it in the episode, but it is in deleted scenes.
那个镜头没能放进正片里，但被收录在删减片段中。

1328
00:57:28.380 --> 00:57:33.800
Well, while the recital is going on, Pam is in the audience and she's filming.
演出进行时，帕姆坐在观众席里拍摄。

1329
00:57:34.300 --> 00:57:35.280
But guess what?
但你猜怎么着？

1330
00:57:36.020 --> 00:57:37.760
She gets a phone call.
她接到了一个电话。

1331
00:57:38.360 --> 00:57:40.500
Yes, and she's so excited.
是的，她非常兴奋。

1332
00:57:40.780 --> 00:57:42.240
It's the city of Scranton.
是斯克兰顿市政府打来的。

1333
00:57:42.340 --> 00:57:45.980
Yes, she got the job painting the mural over Tracy Fleab.
没错，她得到了在特雷西·弗利布画壁画的工作。

1334
00:57:46.100 --> 00:57:47.120
She got the job.
她成功拿下了这份工作。

1335
00:57:47.600 --> 00:57:51.380
Well, the other parents around her are not pleased that she took this phone call.
周围的其他家长对她接电话的行为很不满。

1336
00:57:51.520 --> 00:57:52.160
They're shushing her.
他们都在嘘她。

1337
00:57:52.300 --> 00:57:53.760
They're saying, you are very rude.
他们说，你太没礼貌了。

1338
00:57:53.920 --> 00:57:54.800
Very rude.
非常没礼貌。

1339
00:57:55.180 --> 00:58:00.680
Well, when you watch this, you might think their reactions kind of are harsh, right?
当你看到这一幕时，可能会觉得他们的反应有点过激，对吧？

1340
00:58:01.160 --> 00:58:04.040
There were a few vignettes that led up to this moment.
其实在这之前有几个小片段铺垫了这一刻。

1341
00:58:04.560 --> 00:58:07.440
First of all, Pam tries to get a seat in the front row.
首先，帕姆试图在前排找个座位。

1342
00:58:07.580 --> 00:58:08.460
I remember this.
我记得这个。

1343
00:58:08.580 --> 00:58:09.600
It's in deleted scenes.
在删减片段里。

1344
00:58:09.780 --> 00:58:14.460
And she asks the man she ends up sitting next to if he can move his son.
她问坐在旁边的男人能不能挪一下他的儿子。

1345
00:58:14.660 --> 00:58:17.140
So they put his son on his lap.
于是他们把儿子抱到了腿上。

1346
00:58:17.220 --> 00:58:19.980
His kind of too big-to-sit-on-your-lap son.
那个对他来说有点太大了、不适合坐在腿上的儿子。

1347
00:58:19.980 --> 00:58:20.640
Son, yeah.
没错，儿子。

1348
00:58:20.840 --> 00:58:22.040
To make a space for Pam.
为了给帕姆腾出位置。

1349
00:58:22.120 --> 00:58:23.320
So that's the first thing she did.
所以这是她做的第一件事。

1350
00:58:23.460 --> 00:58:25.880
And then she's trying to get a better shot.
然后她又试图找个更好的拍摄角度。

1351
00:58:25.880 --> 00:58:27.920
And she's kind of like crawling on the floor.
她当时就像是在地板上爬一样。

1352
00:58:28.120 --> 00:58:29.420
Like she's kind of being annoying.
就好像她有点烦人似的。

1353
00:58:29.420 --> 00:58:29.940
All that.
就是那样。

1354
00:58:30.340 --> 00:58:34.040
So by the time she gets the phone call, people have had it with her.
所以等她接到电话的时候，大家已经受够她了。

1355
00:58:34.280 --> 00:58:34.580
Yes.
是的。

1356
00:58:34.960 --> 00:58:37.540
Well, special guest star alert.
好了，特别客串明星预警。

1357
00:58:37.540 --> 00:58:41.160
The angry, shushing mom and dad were played by people we know.
那个愤怒地嘘人的爸爸妈妈是由我们认识的人扮演的。

1358
00:58:41.200 --> 00:58:43.840
But I'll let Kelly Cantley tell you all about it.
但我会让凯莉·坎特利来告诉你们这一切。

1359
00:58:45.020 --> 00:58:47.280
Interesting trivia about the Ladybug recital.
关于瓢虫独奏会的有趣花絮。

1360
00:58:47.280 --> 00:58:54.720
Brian Whittle, our actual boom op for multiple seasons of The Office, plays the man sitting next to Pam.
布莱恩·惠特尔，我们《办公室》多季以来的实际吊杆话筒操作员，饰演坐在帕姆旁边的那个人。

1361
00:58:55.000 --> 00:59:01.820
And then Stephanie Lesh-Farrell, Sean Farrell's wife, one of our set decks, plays the woman sitting next to Brian.
然后斯蒂芬妮·莱什-法瑞尔，也就是我们布景师肖恩·法瑞尔的妻子，饰演坐在布莱恩旁边的那位女士。

1362
00:59:02.420 --> 00:59:07.260
Also, Brian Whittle appears three times in the credits of that episode.
此外，布莱恩·惠特尔在那一集的演职员表中出现了三次。

1363
00:59:07.700 --> 00:59:09.660
Brian's playing the man at the recital.
布莱恩饰演独奏会上的那个人。

1364
00:59:10.000 --> 00:59:14.480
Brian Whittle is also the actual boom operator credited for the show.
布莱恩·惠特尔也是该剧演职员表中真实的吊杆话筒操作员。

1365
00:59:14.480 --> 00:59:21.140
And then Chris Diamantopoulos played Brian Whittle, the boom operator character who breaks the wall.
然后克里斯·迪亚曼托普洛斯饰演了布莱恩·惠特尔，也就是那个打破第四面墙的吊杆话筒操作员角色。

1366
00:59:21.420 --> 00:59:22.740
So there's trivia.
所以这就是花絮。

1367
00:59:24.120 --> 00:59:26.960
Brian Whittle, you're all over the place in this episode.
布莱恩·惠特尔，你在这一集里到处都是啊。

1368
00:59:27.300 --> 00:59:27.380
I know.
我知道。

1369
00:59:27.760 --> 00:59:31.740
I do love that the character of the boom operator's name is Brian Whittle.
我确实很喜欢吊杆话筒操作员这个角色的名字叫布莱恩·惠特尔。

1370
00:59:32.320 --> 00:59:33.740
First and last name.
名字和姓氏都一样。

1371
00:59:33.840 --> 00:59:34.200
I know.
我知道。

1372
00:59:34.220 --> 00:59:35.120
Of the real guy.
是那个真人的名字。

1373
00:59:35.380 --> 00:59:37.980
Of one of the real boom operators for the show.
是该剧真实的吊杆话筒操作员之一的名字。

1374
00:59:37.980 --> 00:59:41.000
You know, this brings me to a fan question from Lindsay A.
你知道，这让我想到了来自加州千橡市的琳赛·A的一位粉丝提问，她说，

1375
00:59:41.080 --> 00:59:43.180
in Thousand Oaks, California, who said,
她说，

1376
00:59:43.320 --> 00:59:46.340
My question is, why is there all of a sudden a boom operator?
我的问题是，为什么突然出现了一个吊杆话筒操作员？

1377
00:59:46.660 --> 00:59:53.100
They've had lapel mics this whole time, and out of nowhere, there's a boom operator who's been doing sound for Pam this whole time.
他们一直都戴着领夹麦克风，怎么突然之间，就冒出了一个一直为帕姆收音的吊杆话筒操作员呢？

1378
00:59:53.940 --> 01:00:01.140
Well, Lindsay, I think this was something that, like, we knew as actors are making a show,
嗯，琳赛，我想这是我们作为演员在制作节目时就知道的事情，

1379
01:00:01.280 --> 01:00:05.620
which is that you wear a mic pack and you have a boom operator.
那就是你会佩戴麦克风包，也会有吊杆话筒操作员。

1380
01:00:05.620 --> 01:00:07.620
It's very common to have both.
两者兼备是非常普遍的。

1381
01:00:07.820 --> 01:00:14.540
They want to have backup sound, and so they grab sound in two different ways on projects.
他们想要备份音频，所以他们在项目中会通过两种不同的方式来收音。

1382
01:00:14.880 --> 01:00:15.400
Always.
总是这样。

1383
01:00:15.580 --> 01:00:15.820
Always.
总是这样。

1384
01:00:16.060 --> 01:00:16.280
Always.
总是这样。

1385
01:00:16.560 --> 01:00:22.080
Even when Josh and I do our little baking videos at home, we have a lav mic kit that we bought,
即使当我和乔什在家里拍我们的小烘焙视频时，我们也会用买来的领夹麦克风套件，

1386
01:00:22.100 --> 01:00:24.280
so we put the little mics on our shirts.
所以我们会把小麦克风别在衬衫上。

1387
01:00:24.560 --> 01:00:26.740
But then he has one boom mic.
但他还有一个吊杆麦克风。

1388
01:00:26.920 --> 01:00:33.040
Basically, he just puts on a tripod because we don't have a person to hold it, so we capture other sound.
基本上，他只是把它放在三脚架上，因为我们没有人来拿它，所以我们能捕捉到其他声音。

1389
01:00:33.040 --> 01:00:37.000
Yeah, you get the atmosphere of the room on the boom mic as well.
没错，吊杆麦克风也能捕捉到房间里的环境音。

1390
01:00:37.260 --> 01:00:37.520
Yeah.
是的。

1391
01:00:37.820 --> 01:00:42.580
And a lot of times, for the most part on our show, it was the boom sound that you heard.
而且很多时候，在我们节目中，大部分时间你听到的都是吊杆麦克风录下的声音。

1392
01:00:42.760 --> 01:00:43.940
The lav mics were backup.
领夹麦克风只是备份。

1393
01:00:44.360 --> 01:00:44.560
Yeah.
是的。

1394
01:00:45.040 --> 01:00:46.620
But it's a really good question.
但这确实是个好问题。

1395
01:00:46.640 --> 01:00:47.340
Good question.
好问题。

1396
01:00:47.720 --> 01:00:53.580
Well, Dwight and Daryl bid farewell to Mr. Romanko, and Dwight asked Daryl if he's ready to tell Jim to go screw himself.
嗯，德怀特和达里尔向罗曼科先生告别，德怀特问达里尔是否准备好告诉吉姆去死吧。

1397
01:00:53.800 --> 01:00:54.860
But Daryl says, No.
但达里尔说，不。

1398
01:00:55.480 --> 01:00:56.640
Athlete is my future.
运动员是我的未来。

1399
01:00:56.920 --> 01:00:58.580
I want to have fun at work.
我想在工作中获得乐趣。

1400
01:00:59.020 --> 01:01:00.660
This gets Dwight's wheels going.
这让德怀特开始动脑筋了。

1401
01:01:00.660 --> 01:01:01.320
Yep.
没错。

