来自斯克兰顿市政府的？

1734
01:12:54.180 --> 01:12:55.600
You're waiting to hear about your mural.
你正等着关于壁画的消息。

1735
01:12:56.140 --> 01:12:57.920
They would have told me in my messages.
他们本可以在留言里告诉我的。

1736
01:12:58.300 --> 01:12:59.820
I would have let it go to voicemail.
我会让它转入语音信箱。

1737
01:12:59.900 --> 01:13:04.600
If I'm filming the recital, the only thing I can think of is if you're so thrown that
如果我在拍摄演出，我唯一能想到的就是如果你太慌乱了，

1738
01:13:04.600 --> 01:13:05.820
you answer by accident.
以至于不小心接了电话。

1739
01:13:06.260 --> 01:13:07.320
She didn't.
她没有。

1740
01:13:07.380 --> 01:13:08.360
She answered on purpose.
她是故意接的。

1741
01:13:08.600 --> 01:13:09.060
That's true.
确实。

1742
01:13:09.280 --> 01:13:14.680
I really thought about this because my instinct was no, I wouldn't answer the phone in the
我真的思考过这个问题，因为我的直觉是“不”，我不会在

1743
01:13:14.680 --> 01:13:18.840
middle of a recital unless it was some indication of an emergency.
演出进行到一半时接电话，除非那是某种紧急情况的信号。

1744
01:13:20.220 --> 01:13:27.820
But as an emerging artist, we get very superstitious, and I could imagine having the anxiety that
但作为一名新兴艺术家，我们变得非常迷信，我能想象那种焦虑感，

1745
01:13:27.820 --> 01:13:30.700
if I don't answer this call, they'll give it to someone else.
如果我不接这个电话，他们就会把机会给别人。

1746
01:13:30.820 --> 01:13:30.920
Right.
没错。

1747
01:13:31.000 --> 01:13:33.560
They'll think I'm unreachable, and they'll pass on me.
他们会觉得我联系不上，然后放弃我。

1748
01:13:33.620 --> 01:13:33.860
Right.
没错。

1749
01:13:34.060 --> 01:13:34.300
Yeah.
是啊。

1750
01:13:34.460 --> 01:13:36.260
So I did understand that.
所以我理解这一点。

1751
01:13:36.360 --> 01:13:36.560
Yeah.
是啊。

1752
01:13:36.680 --> 01:13:37.340
I see that.
我看到了。

1753
01:13:37.680 --> 01:13:42.960
Well, Pam is trying to defend the fact that she took this phone call during the recital,
嗯，帕姆试图为她在独奏会上接电话的事辩解，

1754
01:13:42.980 --> 01:13:45.360
but she doesn't want to say why or who it was.
但她不想说原因，也不想说那是谁打来的。

1755
01:13:45.360 --> 01:13:51.540
So we cut to this talking head where she explains she just wants Jim to be the first one to know
于是镜头切到她的采访，她解释说她只是想让吉姆第一个知道

1756
01:13:51.540 --> 01:13:55.900
about the mural, because whenever something good happens to her, he always says,
关于壁画的事，因为每当她有什么好事发生，他总是会说，

1757
01:13:56.080 --> 01:13:56.560
Beasley!
比斯利！

1758
01:13:57.180 --> 01:13:59.040
And she wants to hear a Beasley.
她想听到那声“比斯利”。

1759
01:13:59.280 --> 01:14:00.220
It's so cute.
太可爱了。

1760
01:14:00.380 --> 01:14:01.120
It's very cute.
非常可爱。

1761
01:14:01.220 --> 01:14:01.660
So sweet.
太甜了。

1762
01:14:01.660 --> 01:14:03.240
We're laying it on thick, guys.
伙计们，我们这煽情过头了。

1763
01:14:03.460 --> 01:14:03.620
Yeah.
是啊。

1764
01:14:04.100 --> 01:14:07.620
Well, now things are just kind of awkward and miserable between Pete and Aaron.
嗯，现在皮特和亚伦之间的气氛变得有些尴尬和难受。

1765
01:14:07.780 --> 01:14:09.120
He's on his way to make copies.
他正要去复印文件。

1766
01:14:09.120 --> 01:14:10.000
She notices.
她注意到了。

1767
01:14:10.000 --> 01:14:11.860
They're kind of curt to one another.
他们对彼此的态度都很冷淡。

1768
01:14:12.600 --> 01:14:14.240
And they both just look unhappy.
而且他们看起来都不开心。

1769
01:14:14.240 --> 01:14:15.860
And Nellie clocks it all.
奈莉把这一切都看在眼里。

1770
01:14:16.400 --> 01:14:16.640
Yeah.
是啊。

1771
01:14:16.980 --> 01:14:19.480
And now Nellie is going to have a meeting with Pete and Aaron.
现在奈莉要和皮特与亚伦开个会。

1772
01:14:19.480 --> 01:14:20.440
And she says, You know what?
她说，你们知道吗？

1773
01:14:20.440 --> 01:14:22.080
I'm going to reassemble the task force.
我要重组特别工作组。

1774
01:14:22.080 --> 01:14:23.040
It's my decision.
这是我的决定。

1775
01:14:23.300 --> 01:14:24.460
They have no choice.
他们别无选择。

1776
01:14:24.640 --> 01:14:25.720
Everybody knows it.
大家都心知肚明。

1777
01:14:26.060 --> 01:14:28.020
She apologizes to them.
她向他们道歉了。

1778
01:14:28.640 --> 01:14:29.980
Aaron and Pete are so happy.
亚伦和皮特非常高兴。

1779
01:14:30.560 --> 01:14:30.720
Yeah.
是啊。

1780
01:14:31.140 --> 01:14:32.680
And Toby approves.
托比也表示赞同。

1781
01:14:32.980 --> 01:14:34.700
He approaches her from behind.
他从背后靠近她。

1782
01:14:34.700 --> 01:14:35.880
He rubs her shoulders.
他揉了揉她的肩膀。

1783
01:14:36.280 --> 01:14:37.640
He calls her lady.
他叫她“女士”。

1784
01:14:38.140 --> 01:14:39.040
Oh, lady.
哦，女士。

1785
01:14:40.000 --> 01:14:41.720
Fan catch from Jessica N.
来自纽约罗切斯特的杰西卡·N的粉丝投稿。

1786
01:14:41.880 --> 01:14:43.220
in Rochester, New York.
她说，哦，不。

1787
01:14:43.420 --> 01:14:44.700
Said, Oh, no.
当托比令人毛骨悚然地从背后靠近奈莉时，他用了那个词。

1788
01:14:45.000 --> 01:14:49.640
When Toby comes up creepily behind Nellie, he uses your hour word.
女士。

1789
01:14:49.860 --> 01:14:50.460
Lady.
不喜欢。

1790
01:14:51.020 --> 01:14:51.700
Dislike.
差评。

1791
01:14:52.900 --> 01:14:54.020
Thumbs down.
倒赞。

1792
01:14:55.620 --> 01:14:56.300
Yeah.
是啊。

1793
01:14:56.520 --> 01:15:00.040
And then he kind of leans in and says, You never stop surprising me.
然后他凑近说，你总是让我感到惊喜。

1794
01:15:00.340 --> 01:15:01.600
Oh, cringe.
哦，尴尬死了。

1795
01:15:02.260 --> 01:15:03.540
Well, here we are, everyone.
好了，各位，我们到了。

1796
01:15:04.260 --> 01:15:05.520
It's the big reveal.
重头戏要揭晓了。

1797
01:15:05.520 --> 01:15:06.100
Yeah.
是啊。

1798
01:15:06.800 --> 01:15:08.800
Is we going to say something else?
我们还要说点别的吗？

1799
01:15:08.800 --> 01:15:09.500
No, it's a big...
不，这是个大……

1800
01:15:09.500 --> 01:15:10.200
It's time.
是时候了。

1801
01:15:10.340 --> 01:15:10.840
It's time.
时候到了。

1802
01:15:10.960 --> 01:15:11.500
It's time.
时候到了。

1803
01:15:12.020 --> 01:15:13.600
Everyone's leaving for the day.
大家都下班走了。

1804
01:15:13.840 --> 01:15:15.340
And Pam gets a phone call.
帕姆接到了一个电话。

1805
01:15:15.660 --> 01:15:16.280
It's Jim.
是吉姆打来的。

1806
01:15:16.680 --> 01:15:17.780
He has bad news.
他带来了一个坏消息。

1807
01:15:17.920 --> 01:15:19.260
They lost Bridgeport Capital.
他们丢掉了布里奇波特资本这个客户。

1808
01:15:19.880 --> 01:15:22.160
I do have a call sheet tidbit here.
我这里有一条关于拍摄通告单的趣闻。

1809
01:15:22.540 --> 01:15:27.120
This scene was the last scene filmed on the last day on Friday.
这一幕是周五最后一天拍摄的最后一个场景。

1810
01:15:27.520 --> 01:15:28.000
Yes.
没错。

1811
01:15:28.140 --> 01:15:29.800
Well, Angela, there was a reason for that.
安吉拉，这其实是有原因的。

1812
01:15:30.000 --> 01:15:35.520
We wanted to clear the set and we wanted to have plenty of time to get this scene because
我们想清空片场，并且想留出充足的时间来拍摄这一幕，因为

1813
01:15:35.520 --> 01:15:36.900
it was complicated.
这很复杂。

1814
01:15:37.360 --> 01:15:38.300
Here's what's going to happen.
接下来会发生这样的事。

1815
01:15:38.300 --> 01:15:40.500
And like I said, Jim says they lost this big client.
就像我说的，吉姆说他们丢掉了这个大客户。

1816
01:15:40.640 --> 01:15:44.040
He says he's going to have to work insanely hard for the next few weeks.
他说接下来的几周他得拼命工作才行。

1817
01:15:44.680 --> 01:15:48.180
Pam has a sort of passive-aggressive comment where she says, Really?
帕姆说了一句带点消极抵抗意味的话，她说，真的吗？

1818
01:15:48.280 --> 01:15:50.700
I feel like you've already been working insanely hard.
我觉得你已经够拼命了。

1819
01:15:51.200 --> 01:15:53.620
Jim says, You know what would make me feel better?
吉姆说，你知道什么能让我感觉好点吗？

1820
01:15:53.620 --> 01:15:56.200
If I could see that video of Cece's recital.
如果我能看到西西那场表演的视频就好了。

1821
01:15:57.000 --> 01:16:01.400
Pam tries to be lighthearted about it and is like, Guess what?
帕姆试图轻松地应对，她说，你猜怎么着？

1822
01:16:01.620 --> 01:16:03.560
Turns out I'm not great with technology.
结果我不太擅长搞这些技术活。

1823
01:16:03.680 --> 01:16:04.820
I didn't get it.
我没录下来。

1824
01:16:05.400 --> 01:16:06.960
Jim is really upset by this.
吉姆对此非常沮丧。

1825
01:16:06.960 --> 01:16:08.060
He's like, Are you kidding?
他说，你在开玩笑吗？

1826
01:16:08.460 --> 01:16:09.540
I mean, come on.
我是说，拜托。

1827
01:16:10.000 --> 01:16:12.180
And Pam's like, You want to ease up a little bit?
帕姆说，你能不能别这么咄咄逼人？

1828
01:16:12.440 --> 01:16:14.620
And then Jim's like, The recital is done.
然后吉姆说，表演已经结束了。

1829
01:16:14.620 --> 01:16:16.060
I missed that moment.
我错过了那个瞬间。

1830
01:16:16.320 --> 01:16:19.620
And she's like, I'm sure another family filmed it.
她说，肯定有别的家庭录下来了。

1831
01:16:19.700 --> 01:16:21.080
A lot of people were recording this.
很多人都在录像。

1832
01:16:21.140 --> 01:16:21.880
And he's like, Oh, great.
他说，哦，太棒了。

1833
01:16:22.000 --> 01:16:27.200
So now I can watch a recording that focuses on their kid and we don't even get to see our kid.
所以现在我只能看别人录的视频，镜头全是他们家孩子，我们连自己孩子都看不到。

1834
01:16:27.660 --> 01:16:28.640
Now they're in it.
现在他们吵起来了。

1835
01:16:28.740 --> 01:16:30.800
Because Pam says, Maybe you should have been there.
因为帕姆说，也许你当时应该在场的。

1836
01:16:31.060 --> 01:16:33.060
Yeah, if it was so important, maybe you should have been there.
没错，如果那件事那么重要，也许你当时应该在场的。

1837
01:16:33.380 --> 01:16:36.420
And he now is ticked off because he says, Listen,
他现在被激怒了，他说，听着，

1838
01:16:36.420 --> 01:16:39.840
Listen, you agreed to me spending these days in Philly.
听着，是你同意我这些天待在费城的。

1839
01:16:40.140 --> 01:16:45.700
And Pam says she's trying to do her best to make things perfect so he can do what he wants to do.
帕姆说她一直在尽力把一切都安排得完美，好让他能去做他想做的事。

1840
01:16:45.840 --> 01:16:48.200
And basically he's like, Oh, this is what I want to do?
而他基本上是说，哦，这就是我想做的事？

1841
01:16:48.280 --> 01:16:49.980
You think I'm just doing this for myself?
你以为我做这些只是为了我自己吗？

1842
01:16:50.520 --> 01:16:52.980
Because if so, then this is a very sad night.
如果是这样的话，那今晚真是个悲伤的夜晚。

1843
01:16:53.260 --> 01:16:54.980
And now Jim is being called back to work.
现在吉姆被叫回去工作了。

1844
01:16:54.980 --> 01:16:55.600
And he's like, You know what?
他说，你知道吗？

1845
01:16:55.600 --> 01:16:56.080
I got to go.
我得走了。

1846
01:16:56.240 --> 01:16:56.980
I'll talk to you tomorrow.
明天再聊。

1847
01:16:57.680 --> 01:16:58.040
Yeah.
嗯。

1848
01:16:58.220 --> 01:16:58.820
She's like, Fine.
她说，行吧。

1849
01:16:59.000 --> 01:16:59.620
Talk to you tomorrow.
明天再聊。

1850
01:17:00.280 --> 01:17:01.860
Pam starts to break down.
帕姆开始崩溃了。

1851
01:17:02.280 --> 01:17:05.080
And this is how it was written in the shooting draft.
这就是剧本初稿里的写法。

1852
01:17:05.680 --> 01:17:06.600
Pam hangs up upset.
帕姆挂断电话，心烦意乱。

1853
01:17:06.900 --> 01:17:10.440
She looks around and realizes she is the only one left at work.
她环顾四周，意识到办公室里只剩下她一个人了。

1854
01:17:10.680 --> 01:17:13.840
She slumps and then unexpectedly starts to cry.
她颓然坐下，随后出人意料地哭了起来。

1855
01:17:14.240 --> 01:17:15.800
We watch her cry for a little.
我们看着她哭了一会儿。

1856
01:17:16.240 --> 01:17:20.380
Then she turns tear-stained face to the side of the room and says,
接着，她转过满是泪痕的脸，看向房间一侧说道：

1857
01:17:20.800 --> 01:17:22.540
Brian, what am I doing wrong?
布莱恩，我到底做错了什么？

1858
01:17:22.740 --> 01:17:23.540
What did I do?
我做了什么？

1859
01:17:24.120 --> 01:17:24.960
There's a beat.
停顿了一下。

1860
01:17:24.960 --> 01:17:27.520
Pam looks like she really needs an answer.
帕姆看起来真的很需要一个答案。

1861
01:17:28.540 --> 01:17:30.480
Brian Whittle responds, Nothing.
布莱恩·惠特尔回答道：什么都没做。

1862
01:17:30.740 --> 01:17:32.080
You're doing the best you can.
你已经尽力了。

1863
01:17:32.360 --> 01:17:35.160
The camera frame quivers, a moment of indecision,
摄像机镜头晃动了一下，似乎有一瞬间的犹豫，

1864
01:17:35.280 --> 01:17:39.900
and then the operator pulls wide to see that Pam is talking to the boom operator, Brian.
随后摄影师拉开镜头，我们才发现帕姆是在和收音师布莱恩说话。

1865
01:17:40.220 --> 01:17:41.540
He looks sympathetic.
他看起来很同情她。

1866
01:17:43.600 --> 01:17:46.800
Fan question from Chloe B in Australia.
来自澳大利亚克洛伊·B的粉丝提问。

1867
01:17:47.220 --> 01:17:50.540
During the phone call between Pam and Jim, Pam is super upset.
在帕姆和吉姆通电话时，帕姆非常难过。

1868
01:17:50.540 --> 01:17:54.980
I was wondering if Jim really was on the other end of the phone during this scene.
我想知道在那场戏里，电话那头真的是吉姆吗？

1869
01:17:55.560 --> 01:17:56.460
Yes, Chloe.
是的，克洛伊。

1870
01:17:56.920 --> 01:18:01.980
Our sound engineer, Ben, hooked it up so that we could actually talk to each other in the two offices.
我们的音响工程师本做了安排，让我们能在两个办公室里真正地进行对话。

1871
01:18:02.360 --> 01:18:07.180
I was on the main stage, and the athlete's set was over in our warehouse building.
当时我在主摄影棚，而运动员的布景在我们的仓库大楼里。

1872
01:18:07.740 --> 01:18:11.520
But setting this up was a huge ordeal, but it was also super important.
虽然搭建这个场景费了很大周折，但它非常重要。

1873
01:18:11.760 --> 01:18:15.300
But I'll let Kelly Cantley, our director, tell you a little more about it.
不过，我还是让我们的导演凯莉·坎特利来为你详细讲讲吧。

1874
01:18:16.200 --> 01:18:18.700
The phone call was so stressful.
那场通话压力太大了。

1875
01:18:19.020 --> 01:18:20.580
There was so much going on.
当时发生了太多事情。

1876
01:18:20.880 --> 01:18:25.800
So normally in television, when we shoot a phone call, we shoot each actor individually.
通常在电视拍摄中，拍摄通话场景时，我们会分别拍摄每位演员。

1877
01:18:26.280 --> 01:18:29.280
So you would shoot one on Tuesday and one on Friday.
比如周二拍一个，周五拍另一个。

1878
01:18:29.280 --> 01:18:34.520
And if you're lucky, the person off camera is actually off camera to give you your cue lines.
如果运气好，镜头外的人会在现场给你对台词。

1879
01:18:34.740 --> 01:18:39.340
But on the office, we did as much live as we could.
但在《办公室》剧组，我们尽可能多地采用现场实拍。

1880
01:18:39.340 --> 01:18:47.400
So anytime we had a FaceTime, we would have a little set over on a corner of the stage, and we'd have an actual live FaceTime.
所以每当有FaceTime通话时，我们都会在摄影棚角落搭个小布景，进行真正的实时通话。

1881
01:18:47.600 --> 01:18:50.180
We tried to do it with phone calls as much as we could.
我们尽可能多地尝试用这种方式处理电话通话。

1882
01:18:50.340 --> 01:18:55.200
And in this case, because the argument was such an important story point,
在这种情况下，因为那场争吵是一个非常重要的剧情点，

1883
01:18:56.160 --> 01:19:00.060
and arguments are sort of better when two people are arguing,
而且两个人吵架时效果往往更好，

1884
01:19:00.060 --> 01:19:06.860
we worked out a way to shoot John playing Jim on the other stage in the athletes set.
所以我们想办法让约翰在另一个摄影棚的运动员布景里扮演吉姆。

1885
01:19:07.260 --> 01:19:11.100
And then Pam, Jenna, was on our regular set.
而帕姆，也就是珍娜，则在我们的常规布景里。

1886
01:19:11.240 --> 01:19:15.400
And there was some technical hoops to jump through to make it happen.
为了实现这一点，我们克服了一些技术上的困难。

1887
01:19:15.740 --> 01:19:22.600
I was on set with Jenna, and Stephanie Kinch, one of the assistant directors, was on set with John.
我和珍娜在片场，而助理导演之一的斯蒂芬妮·金奇则在约翰那边。

1888
01:19:23.240 --> 01:19:28.440
I could see John through the monitor and listen to the dialogue on the Comtex,
我可以通过监视器看到约翰，并通过对讲机听到对话，

1889
01:19:28.580 --> 01:19:30.860
and then in between takes, I could talk to him on the phone.
在拍摄间隙，我还能通过电话和他交流。

1890
01:19:31.700 --> 01:19:35.000
Jenna, I don't know if you remember this, but also on set with us,
珍娜，不知道你还记不记得，当时在片场和我们在一起的，

1891
01:19:35.000 --> 01:19:45.180
it was you, the crew, me, and every producer or executive who'd ever been involved in the office was there.
还有你、剧组人员、我，以及所有参与过《办公室》的制片人或高管都在场。

1892
01:19:46.640 --> 01:19:49.400
Angela, it was not just every producer.
安吉拉，不只是所有制片人。

1893
01:19:49.400 --> 01:19:51.600
It was like every writer.
几乎所有的编剧都在。

1894
01:19:51.600 --> 01:19:54.700
Like, there were so many people.
人真的非常多。

1895
01:19:54.860 --> 01:19:55.620
Greg was there.
格雷格也在。

1896
01:19:56.000 --> 01:19:59.440
So many people invested in us getting this moment right.
有那么多人投入其中，希望我们能演好这一幕。

1897
01:19:59.840 --> 01:20:01.080
It was a lot of pressure.
压力真的很大。

1898
01:20:01.460 --> 01:20:03.600
John was insulated from it a little bit.
约翰受到的影响稍微小一点。

1899
01:20:03.720 --> 01:20:05.060
You were surrounded by it.
而你则被这种压力包围着。

1900
01:20:05.060 --> 01:20:06.080
I was surrounded by it.
我确实被包围着。

1901
01:20:06.140 --> 01:20:09.520
Yes, because our video village was on the main stage.
是的，因为我们的视频监视区就在主舞台上。

1902
01:20:09.640 --> 01:20:09.980
Yes.
是的。

1903
01:20:10.280 --> 01:20:12.140
We got a fan question from Courtney B.
我们收到了来自西澳大利亚州珀斯的 Courtney B. 的粉丝提问，

1904
01:20:12.380 --> 01:20:13.680
in Perth, Western Australia,
西澳大利亚州珀斯，

1905
01:20:13.680 --> 01:20:17.740
who said, I would love to know how you got into character for such an emotional scene.
她问：我很想知道你是如何为这样一场情感戏进入角色的。

1906
01:20:17.740 --> 01:20:23.040
Well, Courtney, this scene really hinged on me being able to break down crying.
嗯，Courtney，这场戏的关键在于我能否崩溃大哭。

1907
01:20:23.340 --> 01:20:32.420
And I'll tell you that in many ways, the writing and the words and the planning of these emotional beats were enough to get me nearly there.
我得告诉你，在很多方面，剧本、台词以及对这些情感节点的规划，已经足以让我接近那种状态了。

1908
01:20:32.420 --> 01:20:43.220
Just playing the truth of the scene to be Pam and having this disconnect from Jim, her true love, that is, like, devastating.
只要演出 Pam 在这场戏里的真实感受，体会与她挚爱 Jim 之间的隔阂，那简直是毁灭性的打击。

1909
01:20:43.540 --> 01:20:45.900
And so that got me nearly there.
所以这让我几乎进入了状态。

1910
01:20:46.140 --> 01:20:51.380
But they really needed me to have tears streaming down my face.
但他们确实需要我泪流满面。

1911
01:20:51.380 --> 01:21:03.460
So what we did was we did a take where John, as Jim, in character, laid into me really hard.
所以我们做的是，拍了一遍，让 John 以 Jim 的角色身份，对我进行了非常严厉的指责。

1912
01:21:03.680 --> 01:21:07.520
It was dialogue that we agreed we would never use.
那段对话我们事先约定好绝不会在正片中使用。

1913
01:21:08.060 --> 01:21:11.240
And they didn't even run the camera on his side.
他们甚至都没有在他的那一侧架设摄像机。

1914
01:21:11.240 --> 01:21:17.420
But through the phone, I just said, you need to get really upset with Pam.
但通过电话，我只是说，你需要对 Pam 非常生气。

1915
01:21:17.720 --> 01:21:20.460
And I'll react as Pam.
而我会以 Pam 的身份做出反应。

1916
01:21:20.460 --> 01:21:27.460
You know, and John was a little nervous about it because he said, this is going to be out of character for Jim, so we can't use it.
你知道，John 当时有点紧张，因为他说，这对 Jim 来说太不符合角色设定了，所以我们不能用。

1917
01:21:28.000 --> 01:21:30.120
But I will do this for you, Jenna.
但我会为你这么做的，Jenna。

1918
01:21:30.340 --> 01:21:31.080
I'll help you.
我会帮你的。

1919
01:21:31.380 --> 01:21:33.360
And I was like, I really appreciate it.
我说，我真的很感激。

1920
01:21:33.420 --> 01:21:35.380
So we turned the camera off on his side.
于是我们关掉了他那一侧的摄像机。

1921
01:21:35.840 --> 01:21:37.660
And it was just him on the phone.
只有他在电话那头。

1922
01:21:37.840 --> 01:21:40.880
So there was that take that you see in the episode.
所以你在剧集中看到的那一遍拍摄，

1923
01:21:41.440 --> 01:21:45.240
That was he, like, really laid into Pam.
就是他真的对 Pam 进行了严厉的指责。

1924
01:21:45.460 --> 01:21:48.060
And I just, it was waterworks.
而我，简直是泪如泉涌。

1925
01:21:48.160 --> 01:21:50.080
And you just reacted as Pam.
而你只是以 Pam 的身份做出了反应。

1926
01:21:50.080 --> 01:21:52.300
So I got there with his help.
所以在他帮助下，我做到了。

1927
01:21:52.720 --> 01:21:52.880
Yeah.
是的。

1928
01:21:53.220 --> 01:21:59.060
I mean, sometimes, you know, in scenes, as your scene partner, you do that for each other.
我的意思是，有时候，作为搭档，你们会为彼此做这些事。

1929
01:21:59.640 --> 01:22:04.240
And even sometimes there'll be a director that will give you a note that just breaks your heart open.
甚至有时候导演会给你一个建议，让你瞬间心碎。

1930
01:22:04.400 --> 01:22:04.660
Yep.
没错。

1931
01:22:04.780 --> 01:22:05.080
You know?
你懂吗？

1932
01:22:05.220 --> 01:22:05.640
That's right.
就是这样。

1933
01:22:05.760 --> 01:22:07.340
And you kind of need it in the moment.
而且你在那一刻确实需要它。

1934
01:22:07.860 --> 01:22:10.840
And then I think, you know, a lot of times you get yourself there.
我想，很多时候你自己就能进入状态。

1935
01:22:11.020 --> 01:22:17.980
But then if you need to dial it up or dial it down, it's really nice to have a scene partner that can help you dial it up emotionally.
但如果你需要加强或减弱情绪，有一个能帮你提升情感强度的搭档真是太好了。

1936
01:22:18.500 --> 01:22:19.780
Well, that was the thing.
嗯，就是这样。

1937
01:22:19.960 --> 01:22:21.580
We had gotten a number of takes.
我们已经拍了好几遍了。

1938
01:22:21.660 --> 01:22:24.100
But we were going to go one more time.
但我们打算再拍最后一遍。

1939
01:22:24.340 --> 01:22:29.140
And I said, okay, for this final one, let her really sob.
我说，好吧，最后这一遍，让她尽情地啜泣吧。

1940
01:22:29.400 --> 01:22:29.620
Yeah.
是的。

1941
01:22:29.620 --> 01:22:30.260
But I need help.
但我需要帮助。

1942
01:22:30.580 --> 01:22:30.740
Yeah.
是的。

1943
01:22:30.740 --> 01:22:35.800
And speaking of that, the first part of this was just getting the fight right.
说到这个，第一部分是把争吵拍好。

1944
01:22:35.900 --> 01:22:39.260
And then the second part was getting this big reveal right.
第二部分是把这个大揭秘拍好。

1945
01:22:39.500 --> 01:22:39.820
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1946
01:22:40.480 --> 01:22:40.740
Yeah.
是的。

1947
01:22:40.900 --> 01:22:45.860
Kelly shared with us about how much planning and discussion went into shooting all of this.
Kelly 和我们分享了拍摄这一切所投入的规划和讨论。

1948
01:22:46.080 --> 01:22:49.340
And also about the different shots that she needed to get.
以及她需要拍摄的不同镜头。

1949
01:22:49.560 --> 01:22:55.440
So not only did she need to make sure all this emotion was happening, but technically she had to make sure she covered it right.
所以她不仅要确保所有这些情感都表现出来，在技术上她还得确保拍摄覆盖到位。

1950
01:22:55.960 --> 01:22:57.140
Here's what she had to say.
听听她是怎么说的。

1951
01:22:58.120 --> 01:23:07.540
Matt and I had come up with a plan for how to block it so that it would be kind of easy to get the camera to Chris, who played Brian the boom-up, when he breaks the fourth wall.
马特和我之前商量好了一个走位方案，这样当饰演收音师布莱恩的克里斯打破第四面墙时，能比较容易地把镜头对准他。

1952
01:23:07.840 --> 01:23:12.860
And then when we rehearsed it, Greg had pictured it very differently.
但当我们排练的时候，格雷格的想法却完全不同。

1953
01:23:13.620 --> 01:23:17.360
So we put everybody in those positions, and we rehearsed it again, and we started to shoot.
于是我们让每个人都站好位，重新排练了一遍，然后开始拍摄。

1954
01:23:17.520 --> 01:23:19.960
And there were lots of opinions on how to shoot it.
关于怎么拍，大家有很多不同的意见。

1955
01:23:20.160 --> 01:23:24.080
And we started shooting it like he was a character.
我们一开始是把克里斯当成一个角色来拍的。

1956
01:23:24.620 --> 01:23:27.460
And we did five or six takes.
我们拍了五六条。

1957
01:23:27.740 --> 01:23:30.040
And Greg said, okay, I think I have what I need.
格雷格说，好了，我觉得我需要的素材已经够了。

1958
01:23:30.300 --> 01:23:32.800
And I said, well, I think I'd like to go one more time.
我说，好吧，但我还想再拍一条。

1959
01:23:32.900 --> 01:23:34.500
And he was like, okay, great, get what you need.
他说，行，没问题，拍到你满意为止。

1960
01:23:35.020 --> 01:23:38.960
Jenna, I came in to talk to you, and you looked up, and hysterically crying because we'd just cut.
珍娜，我走过去找你说话，你抬起头，因为我们刚喊停，你还在歇斯底里地哭。

1961
01:23:38.960 --> 01:23:41.820
And you said, I have one more take in me, and then I'm done.
你说，我还能再拍一条，拍完我就不行了。

1962
01:23:42.020 --> 01:23:45.800
I was like, oh, my God, I felt really bad for asking you to do it again.
我当时心想，天哪，我真为让你再拍一次感到愧疚。

1963
01:23:46.420 --> 01:23:52.820
But we really needed one more because the argument was great, and it ramped up to the point where it was super believable,
但我们确实需要再拍一条，因为那场争吵太棒了，情绪层层递进，真实得让人信服，

1964
01:23:52.820 --> 01:23:58.540
the way two people who love each other can just, like, go at each other.
就像两个相爱的人那样，真的会互相伤害。

1965
01:23:58.720 --> 01:23:59.740
The fight was great.
那场戏拍得真好。

1966
01:24:00.060 --> 01:24:01.600
Your reaction was great.
你的反应也特别棒。

1967
01:24:01.600 --> 01:24:02.600
It was heartbreaking.
让人心碎。

1968
01:24:03.640 --> 01:24:08.780
The only thing that really bugged me is that we were shooting Chris like a character.
唯一让我觉得别扭的是，我们当时把克里斯当成一个角色在拍。

1969
01:24:09.060 --> 01:24:16.300
And I thought that we needed to shoot it like it was found footage, like the doc, you know,
我觉得我们应该把它拍得像纪录片里的那种实拍素材，你知道的，

1970
01:24:16.360 --> 01:24:19.620
they didn't know they were going to show this as part of the doc when it happened.
事情发生的时候，他们并不知道这会被剪进纪录片里。

1971
01:24:19.620 --> 01:24:28.860
So I had had an idea because whenever something, like, disturbing happened or somebody made a noise, a wreck to take,
所以我有个主意，因为每当发生什么令人不安的事，或者有人弄出动静，或者需要重拍时，

1972
01:24:28.960 --> 01:24:35.900
or if a camera person had to give a note, they would, like, shift the camera sort of at a cocked angle on their shoulder
又或者摄影师需要给点提示时，他们会把摄像机从肩上挪开，稍微倾斜一下，

1973
01:24:35.900 --> 01:24:42.280
to make it more comfortable, give the note or tell the person whatever, and then put the camera back up and be ready to go.
这样更舒服些，然后再去给提示或跟人说话，说完再把摄像机扛回肩上准备开拍。

1974
01:24:42.740 --> 01:24:48.860
So I ran in, apologized to you for going again, and said to Matt Sohn,
所以我跑过去，为让你重拍向你道歉，然后对马特·索恩说，

1975
01:24:49.320 --> 01:24:56.900
Matt, this time, as soon as Chris talks, cock the camera onto your shoulder like you're going to yell at me for something
马特，这次克里斯一开口，你就把摄像机从肩上挪开，就像你要冲我喊什么一样，

1976
01:24:56.900 --> 01:25:02.500
and turn to him and say his name or something, like, hey, cut it out, so that it's found.
然后转向他叫他的名字或者说点什么，比如，嘿，别说了，这样看起来才像实拍素材。

1977
01:25:02.500 --> 01:25:05.860
And then once he's in there, you can just cover it because that's what you would do.
等他入画后，你再把镜头跟上，因为这才是你平时会做的。

1978
01:25:06.180 --> 01:25:08.720
So we all agree what we're doing, and we go again.
大家都同意了这个方案，于是我们又拍了一次。

1979
01:25:08.720 --> 01:25:13.980
And I realize once I say action and the scene is going and it's really good,
当我喊开始，戏开拍了，效果非常好，但我突然意识到，

1980
01:25:14.200 --> 01:25:17.260
and then I think, oh, my gosh, I forgot to give him a note about the end.
天哪，我忘了告诉他关于结尾的提示了。

1981
01:25:17.640 --> 01:25:21.540
So I did the worst thing that you can ever do as a director or an assistant director.
于是我做了导演或助理导演最不该做的事。

1982
01:25:21.800 --> 01:25:27.520
I grabbed my AD's radio, Rusty Mahmood, and I turned to the camera channel,
我抓起我的助理导演拉斯蒂·马哈茂德的对讲机，调到摄像频道，

1983
01:25:27.580 --> 01:25:32.320
and on the very last line where Chris, who plays Brian, says, that's enough,
在克里斯（饰演布莱恩）说出最后一句台词“够了”的时候，

1984
01:25:33.100 --> 01:25:38.340
I said, Matt, tilt to the floor so that we're on the floor and you can hear the last line.
我说，马特，把镜头摇向地板，这样我们拍着地板，你还能听到最后那句台词。

1985
01:25:38.720 --> 01:25:39.680
And then you're just out.
然后你就直接出画了。

1986
01:25:40.580 --> 01:25:44.860
So that was very stressful, but I thought the scene came out really good.
那次拍摄压力很大，但我认为那场戏的效果非常好。

1987
01:25:45.020 --> 01:25:48.940
And I thought, Jenna, that you and John did such a good job with the acting of it.
而且我觉得，珍娜，你和约翰的表演都非常出色。

1988
01:25:49.100 --> 01:25:51.440
And Chris was great as the boom-up.
克里斯演收音师也演得很好。

1989
01:25:52.860 --> 01:25:58.600
So that was a really long clip, but I think so fascinating to see how she set that up.
那段视频确实很长，但看到她是如何设计那一幕的，我觉得非常迷人。

1990
01:25:58.600 --> 01:26:02.420
But there were a couple things that she said that stood out to me.
不过她提到的几点让我印象深刻。

1991
01:26:02.740 --> 01:26:09.800
For example, you know, at the end of every take, I'm crying, but now I have to uncry and go back to the beginning.
比如，你知道，每条拍完我都在哭，但现在我得停止哭泣，回到最初的状态。

1992
01:26:10.160 --> 01:26:15.720
And that's the exhausting part, is like taking that journey over and over and over again.
最累人的就是一遍又一遍地经历那种情绪起伏。

1993
01:26:15.720 --> 01:26:19.060
So she was so sweet to be kind of looking out for me.
所以她能那样照顾我，真是太贴心了。

1994
01:26:19.520 --> 01:26:25.180
But then also her brilliant idea to have the camera shift.
还有她那个绝妙的主意，让摄像机位发生偏移。

1995
01:26:25.180 --> 01:26:26.080
Come off the shoulder.
从肩上拿下来。

1996
01:26:26.340 --> 01:26:30.240
Yes, which is what our camera operators did all the time on set.
没错，这正是我们的摄影师在片场经常做的事。

1997
01:26:30.440 --> 01:26:33.580
Yeah, the minute we stopped filming, they would take it off their shoulder.
对，我们一停拍，他们就会把摄像机从肩上拿下来。

1998
01:26:33.580 --> 01:26:35.320
Or if something happened.
或者发生什么突发状况时也会这样。

1999
01:26:35.720 --> 01:26:35.960
Yes.
是的。

2000
01:26:36.660 --> 01:26:38.380
So, so smart.
太聪明了。

2001
01:26:38.880 --> 01:26:42.480
So the boom operator was played by Chris Diamantopoulos.
所以收音师是由克里斯·迪亚曼托普洛斯饰演的。

2002
01:26:42.740 --> 01:26:46.960
At some point, I'm going to share all about him and his casting session for this role.
找个时间，我会好好讲讲他以及他试镜这个角色的过程。

2003
01:26:47.360 --> 01:26:50.220
But I wanted to wait until after the reveal.
但我之前想等真相揭晓后再说。

2004
01:26:50.740 --> 01:26:50.960
Okay.
好的。

2005
01:26:51.420 --> 01:26:54.660
So Brian the boom guy is going to be with us for a little while.
所以收音师布莱恩会和我们待上一阵子。

2006
01:26:54.900 --> 01:26:57.360
I'll tell you all about Chris and how he stole this role.
我会告诉你们关于克里斯的一切，以及他是如何拿下这个角色的。

2007
01:26:57.780 --> 01:27:00.060
You know, obviously I don't ever want to see you cry.
你知道，我当然不想看到你哭。

2008
01:27:00.620 --> 01:27:05.220
But in watching this and re-watching it, at least you look cute when you cry.
但看着这一幕，反复回看时，至少你哭起来的样子很可爱。

2009
01:27:05.580 --> 01:27:06.740
Don't, don't take me wrong.
别，别误会我的意思。

2010
01:27:06.920 --> 01:27:11.040
When I cry and I really like cry, I, it is the ugly cry.
我哭的时候，那种真正的哭，那是真的丑哭。

2011
01:27:11.280 --> 01:27:13.140
Like it is a hot mess.
简直是一团糟。

2012
01:27:13.300 --> 01:27:16.040
And you still look cute.
但你看起来还是很可爱。

2013
01:27:16.620 --> 01:27:17.680
Well, thank you.
好吧，谢谢你。

2014
01:27:17.860 --> 01:27:19.920
I mean, this wasn't an ugly cry.
我是说，这还不算丑哭。

2015
01:27:20.180 --> 01:27:21.820
I can do an ugly cry for you.
我可以为你表演一次丑哭。

2016
01:27:22.020 --> 01:27:28.120
But this was, this was like, oh, this was just, I don't know what.
但这只是，这就像是，噢，我也不知道是什么。

2017
01:27:28.260 --> 01:27:28.780
Heartbroken.
心碎。

2018
01:27:28.780 --> 01:27:31.860
I'm just desperate at the end of my rope.
我只是绝望到了极点。

2019
01:27:32.000 --> 01:27:32.780
And sad.
而且很伤心。

2020
01:27:32.980 --> 01:27:33.260
Yeah.
是啊。

2021
